# Copy to .env (which is git-ignored) and fill in what you need. Every variable is optional:
# the skill itself needs no key of any kind — Wikimedia's pageview and Wikidata APIs are public.
# Values in a real environment variable always win over this file.

# --- Recommended when making live Wikimedia requests --------------------------------------
# Wikimedia's User-Agent policy asks every client to identify itself with contact information
# so operators can reach you if your traffic causes trouble (otherwise they may block it).
# Format: <tool>/<version> (<a URL or mailto: you actually monitor>) <library>
WIKI_INTEREST_USER_AGENT=wikipedia-interest-skill/0.1 (https://github.com/kolibri753/wikipedia-interest) python-urllib

# --- Optional: where cached API responses are stored (default: ~/.cache/wikipedia-interest) ---
# WIKI_INTEREST_CACHE=

# --- Optional: ONLY for the agent evals (evals/harness.py, evals/trigger_eval.py) -------------
# Free tiers, no card required. Not needed to analyze pageviews or build reports.
# Groq:   https://console.groq.com/keys
GROQ_API_KEY=
# Gemini: https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# OpenRouter (optional third provider): https://openrouter.ai/settings/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# --- Optional harness overrides (defaults are per provider in evals/harness.py) ---------------
# MODEL=                 # model id, e.g. gemini-3.6-flash or openai/gpt-oss-120b
# RPM=                   # requests per minute
# TPM=                   # tokens per minute budget (Groq free tier: 8000)
# MAX_REQUEST_TOKENS=    # cap for a single request (defaults to TPM when the tier has one)
